Azure Backup provides a cloud-based approach to protecting supported workloads and recovering data when accidental deletion, corruption, or other failures occur.

Backup planning should consider:

* What data must be protected
* Backup frequency
* Retention requirements
* Recovery objectives
* Backup monitoring
* Restore testing

For example, an organization can back up critical virtual machines according to an established schedule and retain recovery points according to business requirements.

A real-life use case is recovering a business application after an administrator accidentally deletes important files or a system becomes corrupted.

Backup is an important component of business continuity because it provides a recovery mechanism when the original data or workload is no longer usable.
